
Implement the smallest safe read-only configuration
access mechanism for independent TestNG listeners.

The lifecycle adapter already stores the
INVOCATION context UUID in ITestResult.

Requirements:

1. Expose a read-only Supplier<ConfigurationSnapshot>
   through a dedicated ITestResult attribute.

2. Attach the supplier when the INVOCATION context
   is established and the target TEST result is
   available.

3. The supplier must resolve the current snapshot
   using the existing coordinator and invocation UUID.

4. Do not cache the snapshot prematurely.
   Invocation-specific overrides made during
   setup or test execution must remain visible.

5. Do not activate ScopeCursor when resolving.

6. Do not expose the coordinator, registry,
   mutable layers or write operations.

7. Preserve the existing invocation UUID attribute.

8. Keep the supplier available through
   onTestSuccess, onTestFailure and onTestSkipped.

9. After context release, accessing the supplier
   must fail clearly rather than return ROOT values
   or stale configuration.

10. Do not introduce static global mutable state.

11. Do not change listener registration or
    callback ordering.

12. Keep the core independent of TestNG.

13. Do not modify the existing properties manager
    or legacy listeners.

Update the existing real integration test:

- Remove all reflection-based coordinator access.
- Read configuration using the public result attribute.
- Verify success, failure and skipped callbacks.
- Verify parallel invocation isolation.
- Verify updated overrides are visible.
- Verify the absence of active ScopeCursor bindings.
- Verify behavior after invocation cleanup.
- Check both listener registration orders.

Also verify how missing attributes are handled
when a callback has no valid invocation context.

Run the focused tests and full TestNG module.

Report exact results and any remaining limitations.
Keep production changes minimal.













